<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippines details Q1 farm sector growth.</title>
<headline>Philippines details Q1 farm sector growth.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Department of Agriculture on Wednesday gave the following breakdown of production in the Philippine farm sector in the first quarter.</p>
<p>SUB-SECTOR	  PRODUCTION IN THOUSAND METRIC TONNES</p>
<p>MAJOR CROPS	 1995	   1996	    1997</p>
<p>Unmilled rice     2272.05     2523.80	  2577.76</p>
<p>Corn		  1039.15     1043.00	  1026.06</p>
<p>Coconut	     2816.04     2536.41	  2756.06</p>
<p>Sugarcane	   9065.89    10188.11	  11081.22</p>
<p>Banana		743.22	702.59	    718.24</p>
<p>Pineapple	   420.13	389.71	    397.27</p>
<p>Coffee		51.16	 46.35		46.41</p>
<p>Mango		 197.01	186.87	    202.75</p>
<p>Tobacco		21.54	 22.36	     22.25</p>
<p>Hemp		   16.60	 20.01	     16.80</p>
<p>OTHER CROPS</p>
<p>Peanut		 14.17	 13.56	     13.67</p>
<p>Mongo		  12.50	 11.63	     11.75</p>
<p>Cassava		305.90	302.63	   310.56</p>
<p>Camote		 187.73	177.86	   186.17</p>
<p>Tomato		 74.47	  72.56	    72.86</p>
<p>Garlic		 16.31	  17.31	    18.06</p>
<p>Onion		  60.55	  35.23	    37.67</p>
<p>Cabbage		25.36	  18.75	    18.02</p>
<p>Eggplant	     61.90	  62.07	    62.68</p>
<p>Citrus		 13.14	  12.34	    12.86</p>
<p>Rubber		 27.36	  27.65	    26.94</p>
<p>Cotton		 4.18	   5.55		3.52</p>
<p>Fibre crops	  6.60	   6.66		6.61</p>
<p>Others	    1986.58	2071.28	  2093.03</p>
<p>LIVESTOCK</p>
<p>Carabao (buffalo)  23.17	 21.53	     22.96</p>
<p>Cattle		 52.66	 58.19	     62.27</p>
<p>Hog		    290.31	310.63	    329.27</p>
<p>Goat		    16.01	 15.86	     16.07</p>
<p>Dairy		   2.55	  2.58		 2.32</p>
<p>POULTRY</p>
<p>Chicken		183.85	 215.11	    245.23</p>
<p>Duck		   12.43	  13.06		12.70</p>
<p>Chicken eggs	 50.07	  50.50		53.73</p>
<p>Duck eggs	    10.39	  12.00		11.80</p>
<p>FISHERY</p>
<p>Commercial	   207.94     187.50		 191.92</p>
<p>Municipal	    273.79     261.27		 242.09</p>
<p>Aquaculture	  258.66     267.52		 283.99</p>
<p>--MANILA NEWSROOM (63 2) 841-8936, FAX 817-6267</p>
